{
"text": "Online political hostility is positively associated with these indicators, with the strongest associations for political interest, political knowledge, and online participation. These associations are more pronounced for some indicators, especially online and offline participation, among users with more polarized affect directed towards US political leaders. Finally, the results show that engaged but hostile social media users do not simply cater to fringe audiences; they post more frequently and have more friends and followers.",
